On Jan 21, 2:04 am, notarealu...@wireless.co.il wrote:

> I have ascended with a Ki-rin mount before, so I can give you a little
> advice.
>
> 1) Hitting with a wielded potion has the expected effect with all
> healing potions, speed, invisibility, sickness, blindness, and
> paralysis, but others will not have the expected effect, IIRC.
>
> 2) Yes, Ki-rin will pick up and drink useful potions.

Thanks for the advice. I actually did try dismounting yesterday and
dropping three !ofGL at her feet, which she drank. I don't know why I
assumed ki-rin wouldn't drink potions; I guess I was just confused
because my (former) pet angel wouldn't while my archons would, and the
behavior seemed inconsistent.

> But if you want
> a pet to pick up and use useful items, you need to give it no choices
> - trap it at the end of a narrow corridor standing on top of the items
> you want it to pick up and use, with the items in a pile at its feet.
> If it cannot move, it is likely to pick something up pretty quickly,
> and if it is a useful item, it will probably use it instead of
> dropping it.

Right, I've discovered this when trying to equip my other pets. Though
I didn't bother with a corridor this time, and fortunately the ki-rin
still picked up and drank the potions quickly before my archons got to
them. (One of my archons is already level 43 and that's probably quite
enough. ;-) )

> What items are essential for a Ki-rin pet? I equip my ki-rin with the
> following:
> A blessed saddle (the ki-rin can't use that itself, so you need to
> apply it onto the pet)
> an amulet of lifesaving
> a highly enchanted shield of reflection.
> highly enchanted boots, gloves and helmet
> a blessed unicorn horn

Ah, that's good to know that a ki-rin can use all of those things;
she's already saddled, but doesn't have armor or other items. Since I
mounted her right after taming, she didn't have a chance to pick up
and wear any items. I have several spare AoLS and plenty of extra
armor in my stash. Though I just used up all my ?oEA trying to make a
+7 T-Shirt, I'm sure I'll poly up more after the next long round of
sacrificing ;-)

> Keep spare amulets of lifesaving to give to your ki-rin if it uses up
> the one it is wearing.  Use a wand of probing to check its inventory
> and status.
>
> If you are planning on leveling up your ki-rin, note that at a high
> enough level it will become immune to your magic, so you would be
> unable to re-tame it if it goes wild unless you level-drain it.

Yeah, I'm a bit concerned because I've already dismounted her twice
and will need to again to equip her with the above items. I suppose I
should make sure she has everything she needs before giving her any
more !oGL, lest I be completely unable to re-tame her should she go
wild when I dismount...

